    <name>
      <text>real-life-sequence-q3</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>The Environment Club plants trees. Each day it plants the same number of extra trees compared with the day before, so the daily numbers form an arithmetic progression (AP).</p>
<p>The numbers of trees planted on day {@m@}, day {@p@} and day {@q@} are the first three terms of a geometric progression (GP). The club plants {@tot@} trees from day {@m@} to day {@q@}.</p>

<p>(a) Let \(A\) be the number of trees planted on day {@m@}. Use the GP condition to write \(A\) in terms of \(d\).</p>
<p>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>

<p>(b) Find the common difference of the AP  (\(d\)).</p>
<p>[[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>

<p>(c) Find the number of trees planted on day {@m@}.</p>
<p>[[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</p>

<p>(d) Find the common ratio of the GP.</p>
<p>[[input:ans4]] [[validation:ans4]] [[feedback:prt4]]</p>

<p>(e) The GP continues for 4 terms. Find the sum of the first 4 terms of the GP.</p>
<p>[[input:ans5]] [[validation:ans5]] [[feedback:prt5]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>The terms on day {@m@}, day {@p@} and day {@q@} are \( A \), \( A + {@u@}d \) and \( A + {@w@}d \).</p>

<p>(a) <strong>\(A\) in terms of \(d\):</strong></p>
<p>\[ (A + {@u@}d)^2 = A(A + {@w@}d) \]</p>
<p>\[ A^2 + {@2*u@}Ad + {@u^2@}d^2 = A^2 + {@w@}Ad \]</p>
<p>\[ {@u^2@}d^2 = {@k@}Ad \]</p>
<p>Divide both sides by \(d\):</p>
<p>\[ A = \frac{ {@u^2@} }{ {@k@} }d \]</p>

<p>(b) <strong>Common difference:</strong></p>
<p>From day {@m@} to day {@q@} there are {@w+1@} days, starting at \(A\):</p>
<p>\[ S = \frac{ {@w+1@} }{2}\left(2A + {@w@}d\right) = \frac{ {@w+1@} }{2}\left(\frac{ {@2*u^2@} }{ {@k@} }d + {@w@}d\right) = {@c3@}\,d \]</p>
<p>\[ {@c3@}\,d = {@tot@} \qquad d = \frac{ {@tot@} }{ {@c3@} } = {@ta2@} \]</p>

<p>(c) <strong>Day {@m@}:</strong></p>
<p>\[ A = \frac{ {@u^2@} }{ {@k@} } \times {@dv@} = {@ta3@} \text{ trees} \]</p>

<p>(d) <strong>Common ratio:</strong></p>
<p>Day {@p@}: \( {@tm@} + {@u@} \times {@dv@} = {@tp@} \). Day {@q@}: \( {@tm@} + {@w@} \times {@dv@} = {@tq@} \).</p>
<p>\[ r = \frac{ {@tp@} }{ {@tm@} } = {@ta4@} \]</p>

<p>(e) <strong>First 4 terms of the GP:</strong></p>
<p>\[ S_4 = \frac{ {@tm@}\left(\left({@r@}\right)^4 - 1\right)}{ {@r@} - 1 } = {@ta5@} \text{ trees} \]</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
